[#:seon.task{:name "an-escaped-pass-closes-the-reply-without-its-fault"
             :plan "When a turn pass escapes after `seon.fault/fault!` committed, turn-step's finally (agent.clj ~515-558) closes the reply and the caller gets `:seon.await/closed-error` with no fault, although the receipt is on the throw's ex-data (`:seon.fault/recorded`). The causing agent meets the fault only in its next, unrelated run. Offer the recorded receipt (or the fault value) on the reply before closing it. Done when a regression whose pass escapes after recording a fault receives that fault as data in the same reply. The same closed channel meets a second trigger: `seon.turn/settle-batch-refusal!` throws when its own write is refused, the pass rethrows through `seon.turn/close-escaped-run!`, and the caller sees `:seon.await/closed-error` while the fault goes only to root and to the agent's next run; return both refusals as the value ({:refused-outcome :refusal-refused}) and answer them on the reply, and boot recovery closes the run as for any failed terminal write (regression: a refusal settlement that is itself refused answers both refusals as data in its own reply). Read `seon.cluster.agent/evaluate-source!`, `seon.cluster.agent/turn-step`, `seon.fault/carried-receipt` and `docs/research/agent-platform/stability-sweep-2026-09-27.md`."}
