 #:seon.task{:name "a-failed-actions-ownership-is-declared-with-the-action"
  :plan "`seon.cluster.agent/failed-pass!` decides which failed actions end their assignment `:error` with a hand set `#{:attempt :start-flow :merge-base :merge}` over `:seon.flow.actions/op` (held since before 595f8f7de), so an op added to `seon.cluster.agent/assignment-actions` is silently excluded. Done when whether an op's failure ends its assignment is declared once with the ops (the `:seon.flow.actions/op` enum's member properties or the action owner) and `failed-pass!` reads it; the set literal goes. Red proof to write before assignment: a `seon.cluster.db-flow-test` case where a `:close` or `:publish` action throws and the assertion names the declared outcome. Read `seon.cluster.agent/next-actions`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "basis-valid-is-reused-across-unrelated-main-commits"
             :plan "`seon.cluster.agent/basis-valid?` caches under `[(db/commit-id database) sym]` via `seon.cache/lookup ::basis-valid`, so every main commit, related or not, makes every ready leaf's obligations cold. Measured on default with 834 ready leaves (`docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-14/reactive-scheduling.md#2-measurements-default-warm-read-only`): `seon.cluster.agent/launch-facts` 355-370 ms and 341 MB warm, 1.3-2.3 s and 1.4 GB cold; `basis-valid?` alone 1,292 ms and 1,432 MB cold against 3 ms warm, about 1.55 ms and 1.7 MB per ready leaf. What the work must be proportional to: the leaves whose task, ancestors, needs or proofs (what `seon.task/obligations` reads) changed since the last pass, not the leaves times the commits. Key the cache by the content `seon.task/obligations` read (its read evidence or the digests of those entities) so an unrelated commit reuses the value. Proof: to write before assignment (`seon.profile/measure` on `seon.cluster.agent/launch-facts` after one unrelated main commit, on the same 834-leaf probe, against the cold figure)."}
