             :plan "`seon.cluster.agent/taskless-agents` is 94% of an idle `seon.cluster.agent/lifecycle-facts` (11.4 of 12.1 ms and 13.0 MB of 17.3 MB, with one assignment and 3 taskless agents, empty registry; `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-14/reactive-scheduling.md#2-measurements-default-warm-read-only`, finding 3 of `#5-findings-to-file-not-mine-to-fix`). It reads each taskless agent's end and branch head on every pass whether or not anything changed. What the work must be proportional to: the agents whose branch head moved since the last pass, with an unchanged agent answered from its record by head commit id. Change the owner so an idle pass reads no taskless agent's branch. Proof: to write before assignment (`seon.profile/measure` on `lifecycle-facts` with 3 unchanged taskless agents, under 2 ms)."}
 #:seon.task{:name "agent-creation-writes-no-program-namespace"
             :plan "`seon.cluster.agent/creation-tx` creates a program namespace `my.agents.<id>` for every agent, stewarded by it (`:seon.ns/steward`, `steward-call`). Agents are `:seon.data` and never merge, so a chain agent's namespace, born on its chain branch, names an agent main never holds: the final merge excluded it as an interim (`seon.cluster.source/agent-owned`, TASK-CHAIN S3b-1). The owner ruled on 2026-10-14 that namespace agents retire (a task supersedes them). Make agent creation write no program namespace, convert its readers and delete `agent-owned`. Census at e1db21f25 (`rg`): `:seon.ns/steward` 30 lines over 18 files (src: `seon.agent`, `seon.error` twice, `seon.problems`, `seon.db`, `seon.cluster.agent` five sites; schemas `seon.ns.edn`, `seon.agent.edn`); `my.agents.` in 4 src files (`seon.eval.drive`, `seon.cluster`, `seon.sci.eval`, `seon.repl`) and 88 test files; `:seon.agent/namespace` is the agent's REPL namespace, a required ref. Proof: `seon.cluster.merge-test/a-chain-merges-once-and-closes-every-attempt` stays green with `agent-owned` deleted."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-closed-working-attempt-keeps-its-graph"
             :plan "Found by lane open-attempt (2026-10-15), not reproduced. `seon.cluster.agent/launch-actions` makes graphs follow only the open attempts (`seon.task/open-attempt?`: no end, no outcome), so when root closes a chain attempt whose agent is still working (`my.root/close!` → `seon.task/hold-tx`: outcome `:closed`, task `:held`, no end) nothing stops that attempt's graph: it is no longer open, so `follow` never plans its `:stop`. After `my.root/run!` sets the task `:running`, the old agent's `seon.turn/attempt-running?` reads `:running` on the branch again, so it may take turns beside the new attempt's agent; its end then finds no open attempt (`seon.task/agent-attempt` answers nil) and writes only its admission's close. Reproduce in `seon.cluster.db-flow-test/a-capped-chain-attempt-bails-to-root-once-and-root-runs-it-again`: after root closes the second attempt, assert `(str \"attempt/\" key-2)` is no longer under `:seon.agent/started` of the branch's child registry after one pass. Done when db<->flow stops a started graph whose attempt holds an outcome (the attempt rows `seon.cluster.agent/chain-facts` reads already carry it), with that row. Read `seon.cluster.agent/launch-actions`, `seon.cluster.agent/chain-facts` and `seon.task/hold-tx`."}
