             :plan "MERGE-STEP row iii (`docs/seon/schedule/cards/MERGE-STEP.md`, 7e84ba763): `seon.cluster.db-flow-test/a-done-merge-step-merges-its-branch-onto-main` shows a done merge step judged on its merge branch and taken to `seon.merge/merge!` with that branch as source, but its world names no checkout, so the merge stops at `seon.cluster.source/root-refusal`. Done when a world holding a checkout (as `seon.cluster.merge-test` builds one) shows the repaired merge branch accepted onto main, the step's attempt `:merged`, publication by `seon.cluster.agent/finish-chains!` retiring the chain branch and the merge branches its tasks name, and the chain fact retracted. Red-guard triage 2026-10-17 (evidence only, on HEAD db1f01580, three isolated runs): the one red is `db_flow_test.clj:2595`, the reason prefix. Actual reason: 'The final merge refused it.'; expected prefix 'The final merge refused it, :seon.source/write-back-error'. Cause: commit 36c0cfbf2 (2026-10-16 14:35) made the final-merge refusal reason fixed text in the bail in `seon.cluster.agent`, and recorded the refusal type as `:seon.task/refusal` in the same bail transaction; the assertion was not updated. First stored run with this mismatch: candidate 241c8ed09, 2026-10-16 15:16. The earlier red (candidate 04d73ec5a, 2026-10-15 14:19) was another assertion, a check that the kept merge branch is a keyword. Classification: asserts message text, not deleted machinery (no call to the former merge-only judge, deleted in 5f5eb1855; the refusal verdict is `refusals-verdict`). The merge path behaves: the step is kept, appended and judged on its merge branch, and the write-back refusal is expected in this world (no checkout). Stale assertion, not a surviving-path defect; the fix is to assert the refusal type as data. This task also has no `:seon.task/proofs` field, so its Done line names no proof."}
